From c763fedbd0eee325812bef0e59d86b2f16b78be5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flesager <lesager.florian@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:57:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] per: fix APER length determinants and fixed BIT STRING
 alignment

Found with real 3GPP NGAP (TS 38.413) encodings from free5GC; expected
encodings cross-checked with asn1tools 0.169 (aligned PER).

- decode: a bit-field length of a SEQUENCE OF was followed by octet
  alignment; the components follow at once (X.691 11.9.3.3, 20.6). Only
  bit and octet string contents are octet-aligned after their length.
- encode: a length of range 256 or more (one or two octets) was not
  octet-aligned first (X.691 11.5.7.2-3); decode did not align for
  range 256.
- encode and decode: a constrained length requires "ub" less than 64K
  (X.691 11.9.3.3); SIZE(..65536) was treated as constrained.
- decode: a fixed-size BIT STRING of more than 16 bits was not
  octet-aligned (X.691 16.10), unlike what the encoder writes.

tests/issue501.rs asserted the first behaviour for APER; corrected to the
X.691 encoding, which equals UPER for a SEQUENCE OF BOOLEAN.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
